{"id":76,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"The rocklike shell is shed each year. The cast-off shell then crumbles, reverting to a mass of soil, which can be spread across fields to promote crop growth."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Once it sheds its skin, its body turns tender and whitish. Its hide hardens when it’s exposed to air."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It detonates its own body. The power from that explosion can propel it up steep mountain paths with amazing speed."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"When Golem grow old, they stop shedding their shells. Those that have lived a long, long time have shells green with moss."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"Once a year, this Pokémon molts, and its shed shell returns to the soil. This process creates enriched soil, so farmers collect the shells."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Its body can survive dynamite blasts without a single scratch, but it hates rain and humidity."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Golem is known for rolling down from mountains. To prevent them from rolling into the homes of people downhill, grooves have been dug into the sides of mountains to serve as guideways for diverting this Pokémon’s course."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Golem live up on mountains. If there is a large earthquake, these Pokémon will come rolling down off the mountains en masse to the foothills below."},{"games":["Y","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"Even dynamite can’t harm its hard, boulder-like body. It sheds its hide just once a year."},{"games":["X","Pearl"],"text":"It tumbles down mountains, leaving grooves from peak to base. Stay clear of these grooves."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"It is capable of blowing itself up. It uses this explosive force to jump from mountain to mountain."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"It sheds its skin once a year. The discarded shell immediately hardens and crumbles away."},{"games":["Diamond"],"text":"It sheds its hide once a year. Its boulderlike body is so tough, even dynamite can’t harm it."},{"games":["LeafGreen"],"text":"Its boulder-like body is extremely hard. It can easily withstand dynamite blasts without taking damage."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Rock Head","hidden":false,"description":"Protects the Pokémon from recoil damage."},{"name":"Sturdy","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon cannot be knocked out by a single hit as long as its HP is full. One-hit KO moves will also fail to knock it out."},{"name":"Sand Veil","hidden":true,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's evasiveness in a sandstorm."}],"eggGroups":["Mineral"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":15,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium slow","habitat":"mountain","color":"Brown","shape":"Humanoid","evolution":{"id":74,"name":"Geodude","condition":null,"children":[{"id":75,"name":"Graveler","condition":"Lv. 25","children":[{"id":76,"name":"Golem","condition":"Trade","children":[]}]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,33],[1,111],[1,397],[1,484],[16,88],[18,479],[22,523],[24,120],[30,446],[34,350],[40,89],[44,153],[50,38],[54,444]],"machine":[776,34,280,523,174,91,38,414,89,203,263,126,7,53,374,411,264,416,360,912,484,667,63,334,442,118,341,189,182,156,46,350,157,317,201,184,214,479,446,707,444,164,241,36,851,9],"egg":[335,174,223,175,359,5,469],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv9-46","name":"Alolan Golem","set":"Journey Together","date":"2025-03-28","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"46","artist":null,"img":"sv9/46"},{"id":"sv3pt5-76","name":"Golem ex","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Double Rare","number":"76","artist":"Uta","img":"sv3pt5/76"},{"id":"sv3pt5-189","name":"Golem ex","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Ultra Rare","number":"189","artist":"PLANETA Igarashi","img":"sv3pt5/189"},{"id":"swsh8-137","name":"Golem","set":"Fusion Strike","date":"2021-11-12","rarity":"Rare","number":"137","artist":"KEIICHIRO ITO","img":"swsh8/137"},{"id":"sm115-